/T (engineering; it is augmenting it. High-performing modern organizations leverage low-code to clear operational backlogs so senior software architects can focus on core intellectual property. Speed vs. Control Trade-Off: Low-code trades architectural control and fine-grained performance for velocity. Traditional coding trades initial velocity for complete autonomy, zero vendor lock-in, and long-term optimization capabilities.)
